From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] ui/cocoa: drag and drop of files into the VM (drag-drop)

What: with OMACVM_DROP_SOCKET set (the VM's drag-drop switch is on), every
VM window (the main view in every mode, each display head) is a drop target
for file URLs. A drag is taken (copy) only while the app's side said
"ready" (the VM's omacvm-drop answers), with 1-256 files and no folder
(ui/omacvm-drop.h); the guest's pointer follows the drag (omacvmQueuePointer).
performDragOperation returns at once: a serial utility queue opens the files
(O_NOFOLLOW, regular files only, 30 s for a drop) and sends them, open, with
their names to the app over the socket (SCM_RIGHTS, 32 per frame). No path
leaves QEMU. OMACVM_DROP_TEST=1 also takes the app's "test-drop" lines,
which run the same code as a drop after the pasteboard (the hidden VM rows).
Without OMACVM_DROP_SOCKET nothing of this runs: no drop types, as before.

Why: QEMU is the process the person drops on, so macOS gives it, and only
it, access to the dropped files (no prompt for Desktop or Documents); opening
off the main thread keeps the window drawing while an iCloud file downloads.

Upstream: not applicable (OmacVM.app's drop share and port, ADR 0069).
Test: app/runtime/Tests/drop/test-drop.sh (rules and wiring), the hidden VM
rows src/tests/e2e/drag-drop.sh.

